      "writtenOn": "2021-09-03T03:04:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think there is any behavior changed here. You can look at the netd code below, netd check the traffic permissions by app id not by uid. Besides, the uids getting from startMonitoring() are base uids(app ids) because the user in mPackageManager is always primary user and we don\u0027t combine the user ids when sending these app ids to netd either. So we are sending app ids traffic permissions to netd actually.\n* https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/system/netd/server/TrafficController.cpp?q\u003d%22mPrivilegedUser.find(appId)%22\u0026sq\u003dpackage:aosp-master\n\n* https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/system/netd/bpf_progs/netd.c;l\u003d359\n\nI think the question is what kind of value (uid or app id) should bring to INetd#trafficSetNetPermForUids \n* If app id, we should rename it to INetd#trafficSetNetPermForAppIds. And this patch also rename the related methods.\n* If uid, renaming traffic permissions related methods is totally incorrect in this patch. We should combine user id with each uid before sending them to netd. But this should be a large behavior change indeed.\n\nI prefer go second one to send uid\u0027s traffic permission because we are going to save uid\u0027s network permissions in aosp/1773890, maybe traffic permissions will have similar requirement in the furture. Even netd only check permission by app id now, have uid\u0027s permission in hand we can update the design to check uid permission anytime if needed. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "da1c4b93_531af5ff",
